sdk_examples:
Quick pseudo-API (JS):

const client = Redwood.hosted({ apiKey: KEY, samples: [sample1, sample2] })
await client.onramp() // returns typedStencil
const session = client.stream({ model: 'rwd-compact-v1', sessionPrefs: { latencyBudgetMs: 120 } })
session.on('fragment', (f) => renderFragment(f))
// tool call: returns optimistic placeholder, then confirmed or compensated
const call = await session.callTool('calendar.create', { date: '2026-01-12' }, { idempotencyKey: 'abc' })
// call may emit: {type: 'tool-op', id: 't-123', state: 'optimistic' } then 'confirmed' or 'compensated'

Notes to SDK implementer: keep default exports minimal; expose advanced knobs only behind feature flags. Provide small CLI to capture samples from playground and produce sample bundle for onramp.
